<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Succession crisis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A succession crisis refers to the recurring pattern in which disputes over who should inherit power weakened empires. Lacking clear rules, rival heirs often fought civil wars. Examples include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>.</p></div>
